{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And they did so.</b> Immediately before they journeyed, and the impure persons, when they journeyed, would journey between the standard of Ephraim and the standard of Dan, by way of reasoning, for it is not specified. And the section of a man or a woman is juxtaposed because leprosy and flux come on account of trespass. And the reason to mention this section a second time is to mention 'and if a man has no redeemer.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:22.030955244Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}